    "project": "Calibrated Concept-Based Feedback Model (CSE 4385)",
    "description": "Authoritative canonical 112-concept CUB benchmark mapping from Koh et al. (ICML 2020)",
    "source_repository": "https://github.com/yewsiang/ConceptBottleneck",
    "source_file": "https://github.com/yewsiang/ConceptBottleneck/blob/master/CUB/generate_new_data.py",
    "paper_citation": "Koh, P. W., Nguyen, T., Tang, Y. S., Mussmann, S., Pierson, E., Kim, B., & Liang, P. (2020). Concept Bottleneck Models. Proceedings of the 37th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML).",
    "num_concepts": 112,
    "indexing_convention_note": "concept_index is 0..111 in the concept bottleneck vector. zero_based_column_index is 0..311 corresponding to Python array column indexing in Koh et al. cub_attribute_id is 1..312 corresponding to the official 1-based ID in CUB_200_2011/attributes.txt (cub_attribute_id = zero_based_column_index + 1).",
    "selection_procedure_summary": "Derived from the canonical benchmark of Koh et al. (2020) and reused in Shin et al. (2023), Vandenhirtz et al. (2024), and Kalampalikis et al. (2026). Filters raw 312 attributes to 112 active concepts based on class-level presence across species."
